ngx_http_zstd_static_module of nginx-zstd-module (sysadmin-labs 0.1.3) back (aZ,
22.11.2026: all three static modules, .zst before .br), as a module of its own
(--add-module=<module>/static after ngx_brotli in the Makefile: its handler is
then registered after that of brotli_static and nginx calls it first; from the
config of the module it stood before brotli_static and a client of "zstd, br" got
the .br), so its source one directory up. In the module:
- the q-values of Accept-Encoding, as in the filter
  (extra-patch-zstd-accept-encoding): "zstd;q=0" got the .zst file;
- r->gzip_tested and r->gzip_ok left alone: set to "tested, not ok" for a client
  that takes zstd, they kept the gzip filter from a response without a .zst file
  that the zstd filter does not compress (zstd off there, or another type), and
  the client of "zstd, gzip" got it as it is;
- h->next of its Content-Encoding line set (NULL), as nginx does since 1.23.0 for
  every line it makes (ngx_http_gzip_static_module.c).
Applied by post-patch in WRKSRC_zstd, -p0.

